# Chatbot AI: Lumi (/api/ai/chat) and the AI exercise/challenge generator.
# Separate on purpose from NVIDIA_CODE_JUDGE_API_KEY above, which grades Arcade
# round code - do not point both at one model, the judge runs on every round of
# every live match and its token budget is not spare capacity.
# Local dev only, do not commit.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=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
#
# Model: nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b, set 2026-08-25 (แทน moonshotai/kimi-k3).
# คนละคีย์และคนละโมเดลกับตัวตรวจโค้ด (nemotron-3-super-120b) เสมอ
#
# The third model this project has had to replace because the provider stopped
# serving it. z-ai/glm-5.2 began returning 410, deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash-0731
# accepts a request and never returns a token, and moonshotai/kimi-k2.6 - which
# Person 2's server was still configured to use - returns 404 on their own key as
# well as ours, so their chatbot had been silently falling back for some time.
# kimi-k3 is the successor to k2.6 and was verified working on both keys.
#
# All three failed while listed in NVIDIA's catalogue, so presence in models.list()
# proves nothing - send a real request when checking. Changing model is this one
# line; nothing in code needs to change.
NVIDIA_AI_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b
# How long to wait for a reply before falling back, in ms.
# Raised from 45s to 90s on 2026-08-25. kimi-k3's latency on NVIDIA's hosted
# endpoint varies a lot for the same prompt - three identical requests took
# 1.4s, 7.4s and 14.1s - and the spread is server-side load, not our token
# budget (the largest request was the fastest of the three). 90s leaves room
# for the slow tail rather than turning it into an error the user sees.
NVIDIA_AI_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
